# AMR-WB 3GPP TS 26.173 ANSI-C fixed-point reference. Fetched (3gpp.org) to *port* to pure Rust —
# read as the algorithm reference, never compiled and never committed (3GPP licensing + bloat).
amr-wb/c-code/

# The official test vectors (testv/: tst_mN.cod bitstreams + tst_mN.out decoded PCM) are the
# bit-exact acceptance criteria. They are kept untracked until git-lfs is configured for them, then
# committed via LFS; they must never enter normal git history as binaries.
amr-wb/testv/

# The third-party X2/X3 Wireshark dissector used as an independent decoder for the TS 103 221-2
# framing. Fetched by x2x3-dissector/fetch.sh against a pinned SHA-256, never committed — it is
# someone else's code under its own licence. Tests skip-when-absent.
x2x3-dissector/x2x3PduDissector.lua

# Opus RFC 6716 conformance reference data — the official testvectorNN.bit/.dec, the locally
# generated CELT-only oracle vectors (celt_only/, from a libopus OPUS_SET_FORCE_MODE oracle), and any
# libopus source/oracle build artifacts. All reference-only acceptance data: never committed (bloat +
# licensing), kept untracked like the AMR-WB vectors. Tests skip-when-absent.
# No trailing slash: the tree is big enough that it is normally built once and reached from a
# secondary checkout through a symlink, which a directory-only pattern would not match.
opus
